  "worked_solution": "First, let\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{3}{n({n}^{2}+4)}\\,\\text{and}\\,{b}_{n}=\\frac{3(-1)^{n+1}}{n({n}^{2}+4)}.\n$$\n\nThen ${a}_{n}$ is decreasing for $n\\ge 2$ and ${a}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty .$ Therefore, the series is convergent by the alternating series test.\n\nBecause the series is a convergent alternating series, the alternating series error bound applies. In particular, for the $i$th partial sum, it states that\n\n$$\n|S-{s}_{i}|<|{b}_{i+1}|.\n$$\n\nThus, we require\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{b}_{i+1}|=|\\frac{3(-1)^{i+2}}{(i+1)((i+1)^{2}+4)}| & \\le 0.05 \\\\ \\frac{3}{(i+1)((i+1)^{2}+4)} & \\le \\frac{1}{20} \\\\ 60 & \\le (i+1)((i+1)^{2}+4) \\\\ 60 & \\le (i+1)({i}^{2}+2i+1+4) \\\\ 60 & \\le (i+1)({i}^{2}+2i+5) \\\\ 60 & \\le {i}^{3}+3{i}^{2}+7i+5 \\\\ {i}^{3}+3{i}^{2}+7i+5 & \\ge 60.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
